cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SHIMA-Python in your work, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "SHIMA-Python: Single-cell Heterogeneity and Interactive Molecular Analysis"
type: software
version: "1.0.1"
repository-code: "https://github.com/msherafatian/shima-python"
url: "https://github.com/msherafatian/shima-python"

authors:
  - family-names: Sherafatian
    given-names: Masih
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2814-6036"

abstract: >
  SHIMA-Python is a Python/Dash/Scanpy implementation for interactive
  single-cell RNA sequencing analysis. It provides quality control,
  clustering, marker-gene analysis, functional pathway scoring, trajectory
  inference, cell-cycle analysis, and export of publication-ready figures
  and data.

keywords:
  - single-cell RNA-seq
  - scRNA-seq
  - cancer bioinformatics
  - trajectory inference
  - tumor heterogeneity
  - Dash
  - Scanpy
  - SHIMA
  - Louvain
  - Leiden
  - CancerSEA

license: GPL-3.0-or-later
